// ============================================================================
// Character Builder — randomized customer avatars
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Built from Character_Build.svg. There are TWO hairSTYLES (girl / boy), and
// within each style, several complete alternate hairstyle VARIANTS drawn as
// separate paths (Girl-Hair-1..6, Boy-Hair-1..5) -- only ONE variant is ever
// shown at a time, never stacked.
//
// HOW IT WORKS
// The SVG below is a template string with {{PLACEHOLDER}} tokens instead of
// hardcoded values:
//   {{SHIRT_COLOR}}              - fill for the shirt
//   {{SKIN_COLOR}}               - fill for the face/skin
//   {{HAIR_COLOR}}               - fill used by whichever single hair variant
//                                  ends up visible (randomized independently
//                                  of hair style/variant -- see DEFAULT_HAIR_COLORS)
//   {{GIRL_HAIR_1_DISPLAY}} .. {{GIRL_HAIR_6_DISPLAY}}  - 'inline' or 'none',
//                                  exactly one of these six is 'inline'
//   {{BOY_HAIR_1_DISPLAY}} .. {{BOY_HAIR_5_DISPLAY}}    - 'inline' or 'none',
//                                  exactly one of these five is 'inline'
//   {{MOUTH_STRAIGHT_DISPLAY}} / {{MOUTH_SMILE_DISPLAY}} - 'inline' or 'none'
//
// Every customer spawns smiling. The two mouth shapes also carry stable
// classes (.cb-mouth-straight / .cb-mouth-smile) so setCharacterMouth() can
// switch a customer to the straight/worried mouth later -- e.g. once their
// patience timer drops into its last few seconds -- without regenerating the
// whole character.
//
// generateCharacterSVG(config) fills in those tokens and returns a ready-to-
// insert SVG string -- assign it to a .customer-face element's innerHTML.
// randomCharacterConfig(shirtColors, skinTones, hairColors) picks a random combination.
// createRandomCharacterSVG(shirtColors, skinTones, hairColors) does both in one call.
// setCharacterMouth(container, mouthStyle) swaps the mouth after the fact.
// ============================================================================

